{"sounds":{"intro":"Finnish is written in the Latin alphabet and is spelled exactly as it sounds. It is not related to Swedish or Russian. There are no genders and no articles. Words are long because endings pile up. The stress is always on the first syllable.","rows":[["ä","like \"a\" in \"cat\"","äiti"],["ö","say \"ur\" with rounded lips, like \"ur\" in \"fur\"","työ"],["y","say \"ee\" with rounded lips, like German \"ü\"","yö"],["aa / ee / ii / oo / uu / yy","a double vowel is held long","maa"],["kk / pp / tt / ss","a double consonant is held long, with a pause before it","kukka"],["r","rolled, as in Spanish or Italian","rakas"],["h","breathy, always said","hei"],["ng","like \"ng\" in \"finger\" (both sounds are said)","kenkä"]],"notes":["Double letters change the meaning. \"Tuli\" is fire, \"tuuli\" is wind, \"tulli\" is customs.","Vowel harmony: a word uses either back vowels (a, o, u) or front vowels (ä, ö, y) in its endings, never both. Talossa (in the house), kylässä (in the village)."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","nolla","NOL-lah"],["one","yksi","EWK-si"],["two","kaksi","KAHK-si"],["three","kolme","KOL-meh"],["four","neljä","NEL-yah"],["five","viisi","VEE-si"],["six","kuusi","KOO-si"],["seven","seitsemän","SAYT-seh-mahn"],["eight","kahdeksan","KAHH-dek-sahn"],["nine","yhdeksän","EWH-dek-sahn"],["ten","kymmenen","KEW-meh-nen"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","yksitoista","EWK-si-toy-stah"],["twelve","kaksitoista","KAHK-si-toy-stah"],["thirteen","kolmetoista","KOL-meh-toy-stah"],["fourteen","neljätoista","NEL-yah-toy-stah"],["fifteen","viisitoista","VEE-si-toy-stah"],["sixteen","kuusitoista","KOO-si-toy-stah"],["seventeen","seitsemäntoista","SAYT-seh-mahn-toy-stah"],["eighteen","kahdeksantoista","KAHH-dek-sahn-toy-stah"],["nineteen","yhdeksäntoista","EWH-dek-sahn-toy-stah"],["twenty","kaksikymmentä","KAHK-si-kewm-men-tah"]]},{"id":"tens","title":"Tens","items":[["ten","kymmenen","KEW-meh-nen"],["twen