h-tah"],["to translate","kääntää","KAHN-tah"],["to graduate","valmistua","VAHL-mis-too-ah"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Finnish has no he / she difference: \"hän\" means both. In speech people often use \"se\" (it) for a person and \"me\" or \"mä\" for I. \"Sinä\" is you (informal) and \"te\" is you (formal or plural)."],"rows":[["I","minä","MI-nah"],["you (informal)","sinä","SI-nah"],["he / she","hän","hahn"],["we","me","meh"],["you (formal or plural)","te","teh"],["they","he","heh"]],"ex":[["I am a student","minä olen opiskelija","MI-nah O-len OP-pis-keh-li-yah"],["you are tall","sinä olet pitkä","SI-nah O-let PIT-kah"],["she is my older sister","hän on isosiskoni","hahn on I-so-sis-ko-ni"],["we are friends","me olemme ystäviä","meh O-lem-meh EWS-tah-vi-ah"],["they are teachers","he ovat opettajia","heh O-vaht OP-pet-tah-yi-ah"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Add -t to the noun for the plain plural: kirja, kirjat. After a number, the noun stays singular and takes the \"-a / -ä\" ending: kaksi kirjaa (two books)."],"rows":[["kirja (book)","kirjat","KIR-yaht"],["talo (house)","talot","TAH-lot"],["lapsi (child)","lapset","LAHP-set"],["kissa (cat)","kissat","KIS-saht"],["after a number","kaksi kirjaa","KAHK-si KIR-yah"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","yksi talo, talot","EWK-si TAH-lo, TAH-lot"],["one book, books","yksi kirja, kirjat","EWK-si KIR-yah, KIR-yaht"],["one cat, cats","yksi kissa, kissat","EWK-si KIS-sah, KIS-saht"],["two books","kaksi kirjaa","KAHK-si KIR-yah"],["the children","lapset","LAHP-set"]]},{"id":"to-be-olla","title":"To be: olla","text":["Learn the six forms: olen, olet, on, olemme, olette, ovat. In the third person, \"on\" is used for both singular and plural in speech."],"rows":[["I am","olen","O-len"],["you are","olet","O-let"],["he / she is","on","on"],["we are","olemme","O-lem-meh"],["you are (formal or plural)","olette","O-let-teh"],["they are","ovat","O-vaht"]],"ex":[["I am a student","olen opiskelija","O-len OP-pis-keh-li-yah"],["you are tired","olet väsynyt","O-let VAH-sew-newt"],["he is a doctor","hän on lääkäri","hahn on LAH-ah-kah-ri"],["we are happy","olemme onnellisia","O-lem-meh ON-nel-li-si-ah"],["they are at home","he ovat kotona","heh O-vaht KO-to-nah"]]},{"id":"having-minulla-on","title":"Having: minulla on","text":["Finnish has no verb \"to have\". It says \"at me is\": minulla on (I have), sinulla on (you have), hänellä on (he has). The thing owned is the subject."],"rows":[["I have","minulla on","MI-nool-lah on"],["you have","sinulla on","SI-nool-lah on"],["he / she has","hänellä on","HAH-nel-lah on"],["we have","meillä on","MAY-lah on"],["I do not have","minulla ei ole","MI-nool-lah ay O-leh"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","minulla on isoveli","MI-nool-lah on I-so-veh-li"],["I have a car","minulla on auto","MI-nool-lah on OW-to"],["I do not have time","minulla ei ole aikaa","MI-nool-lah ay O-leh AH-ee-kah"],["there is a problem","on ongelma","on ON-gel-mah"],["there is no water","vettä ei ole","VET-tah ay O-leh"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["Take the infinitive, drop the ending, and add the person ending. Puhua (to speak): puhun, puhut, puhuu, puhumme, puhutte, puhuvat."],"rows":[["I speak","puhun","POO-hoon"],["you speak","puhut","POO-hoot"],["he / she speaks","puhuu","POO-hoo"],["we speak","puhumme","POO-hoom-meh"],["you speak (formal)","puhutte","POO-hoot-teh"],["they speak","puhuvat","POO-hoo-vaht"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","syön leipää","SEW-urn LAY-pah"],["you speak English","puhut englantia","POO-hoot EN-glahn-ti-ah"],["he is reading a book","hän lukee kirjaa","hahn LOO-keh KIR-yah"],["we live in Tashkent","asumme Taškentissa","AH-soom-meh TAHSH-ken-tis-sah"],["they work at school","he työskentelevät koulussa","heh TEW-urs-ken-teh-leh-vaht KOW-loos-sah"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The usual order is who, verb, what. Finnish has no articles, so there is no \"the\" or \"a\"."],"rows":[["I read a book","luen kirjan","LWEN KIR-yahn"],["I drink tea","juon teetä","YWON TAY-tah"],["She reads","hän lukee","hahn LOO-keh"],["We study","opiskelemme","OP-pis-keh-lem-meh"]],"ex":[["I like coffee","pidän kahvista","PI-dan KAH-hvis-tah"],["she is learning Finnish","hän opiskelee suomea","hahn OP-pis-keh-leh SWOH-meh-ah"],["we are going to school","menemme kouluun","MEH-nem-meh KOW-loon"],["I need water","tarvitsen vettä","TAR-vit-sen VET-tah"],["the teacher is here","opettaja on täällä","OP-pet-tah-yah on TAH-ahl-lah"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Finnish has a negative verb, \"ei\", which changes with the person: en, et, ei, emme, ette, eivät. The main verb stays in its short form after it."],"rows":[["I do not go","en mene","en MEH-neh"],["you do not go","et mene","et MEH-neh"],["he / she does not go","ei mene","ay MEH-neh"],["we do not go","emme mene","EM-meh MEH-neh"],["they do not go","eivät mene","AY-vat MEH-neh"]],"ex":[["I want","haluan","HAH-loo-ahn"],["I do not want","en halua","en HAH-loo-ah"],["I speak English","puhun englantia","POO-hoon EN-glahn-ti-ah"],["I do not speak English","en puhu englantia","en POO-hoo EN-glahn-ti-ah"],["I like it","pidän siitä","PI-dan SEE-tah"],["I do not like it","en pidä siitä","en PI-dah SEE-tah"],["she is here","hän on täällä","hahn on TAH-ahl-lah"],["she is not here","hän ei ole täällä","hahn ay O-leh TAH-ahl-lah"],["I have a car","minulla on auto","MI-nool-lah on OW-to"],["I do not have a car","minulla ei ole autoa","MI-nool-lah ay O-leh OW-to-ah"],["I understand","ymmärrän","EWM-mahr-rahn"],["I do not understand","en ymmärrä","en EWM-mahr-rah"],["we are tired","olemme väsyneitä","O-lem-meh VAH-sew-nay-tah"],["we are not tired","emme ole väsyneitä","EM-meh O-leh VAH-sew-nay-tah"],["he works on Sundays","hän työskentelee sunnuntaisin","hahn TEW-urs-ken-teh-leh SOON-noon-tah-ee-sin"],["he does not work on Sundays","hän ei työskentele sunnuntaisin","hahn ay TEW-urs-ken-teh-leh SOON-noon-tah-ee-sin"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add -ko or -kö to the first word and move it to the front: Puhutko? (Do you speak?). Or use a question word."],"rows":[["Do you speak English?","puhutko englantia?","POO-hoot-ko EN-glahn-ti-ah"],["Is he at home?","onko hän kotona?","ON-ko hahn KO-to-nah"],["Do you have a pen?","onko sinulla kynä?","ON-ko SI-nool-lah KEW-nah"]],"ex":[["do you understand?","ymmärrätkö?","EWM-mahr-rat-ko"],["is this a book?","onko tämä kirja?","ON-ko TAH-mah KIR-yah"],["are you a student?","oletko opiskelija?","O-let-ko OP-pis-keh-li-yah"],["do you like tea?","pidätkö teestä?","PI-dat-ko TAYS-tah"],["can you help me?","voitko auttaa minua?","VOY-tko OW-tah-ah MI-noo-ah"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words go at the start of the sentence."],"rows":[["who","kuka","KOO-kah"],["what","mikä / mitä","MI-kah / MIT-ah"],["where","missä","MIS-sah"],["when","milloin","MIL-loyn"],["why","miksi","MIK-si"],["how","miten","MI-ten"],["how much","paljonko","PAHL-yon-ko"]],"ex":[["who is he?","kuka hän on?","KOO-kah hahn on"],["where is the school?","missä koulu on?","MIS-sah KOW-loo on"],["when is the lesson?","milloin tunti on?","MIL-loyn TOON-ti on"],["why are you late?","miksi olet myöhässä?","MIK-si O-let MEW-ur-has-sah"],["how much is it?","paljonko se maksaa?","PAHL-yon-ko seh MAHK-sah"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Add an ending to the noun: -ni (my), -si (your), -nsa / -Vn (his, her), -mme (our), -nne (your, plural), -nsa (their). Often \"minun\" or \"sinun\" is added: minun kirjani."],"rows":[["my book","kirjani","KIR-yah-ni"],["your book","kirjasi","KIR-yah-si"],["his / her book","hänen kirjansa","HAH-nen KIR-yahn-sah"],["our book","kirjamme","KIR-yahm-meh"],["your book (plural)","kirjanne","KIR-yahn-neh"]],"ex":[["my mother is a teacher","äitini on opettaja","AH-ee-ti-ni on OP-pet-tah-yah"],["I like music","pidän musiikista","PI-dan MOO-see-kis-tah"],["she likes dogs","hän pitää koirista","hahn PI-tah KOY-ris-tah"],["this is our school","tämä on koulumme","TAH-mah on KOW-loom-meh"],["your name is nice","nimesi on kaunis","NI-meh-si on KOW-nis"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["sinä (informal): friends, family, children, and most people today. te (formal): older strangers, some work situations. In Finland people use \"sinä\" almost everywhere, even with teachers."],"rows":[["how are you? (informal)","mitä kuuluu?","MIT-ah KOO-loo"],["how are you? (formal)","mitä teille kuuluu?","MIT-ah TAYL-leh KOO-loo"],["are you tired? (informal)","oletko väsynyt?","O-let-ko VAH-sew-newt"],["are you tired? (formal)","oletteko väsynyt?","O-let-teh-ko VAH-sew-newt"]],"ex":[["can you help me?","voitko auttaa minua?","VOY-tko OW-tah-ah MI-noo-ah"],["can you help me? (formal)","voitteko auttaa minua?","VOY-tteh-ko OW-tah-ah MI-noo-ah"],["where are you from?","mistä olet kotoisin?","MIS-tah O-let KO-toy-sin"],["where are you from? (formal)","mistä olette kotoisin?","MIS-tah O-let-teh KO-toy-sin"],["what is your name?","mikä sinun nimesi on?","MI-kah SI-noon NI-meh-si on"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: usually add -i- to the stem: puhun, puhuin (I spoke). Future: Finnish has no future tense. Use the present with a time word: menen huomenna (I go tomorrow)."],"rows":[["I spoke","puhuin","POO-hoo-in"],["I was","olin","O-lin"],["I went","menin","MEH-nin"],["I will go","menen huomenna","MEH-nen HWOH-men-nah"]],"ex":[["yesterday I read a book","eilen luin kirjan","AY-len LOO-in KIR-yahn"],["we were at school","olimme koulussa","O-lim-meh KOW-loos-sah"],["tomorrow I will study","huomenna opiskelen","HWOH-men-nah OP-pis-keh-len"],["he went home","hän meni kotiin","hahn MEH-ni KO-teen"],["I did not go","en mennyt","en MEN-newt"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: the stem alone (tule!). Formal or plural: add -kaa / -kää (tulkaa!). To forbid, use \"älä\": älä tule!"],"rows":[["come!","tule!","TOO-leh"],["come! (formal)","tulkaa!","TOOL-kah"],["wait!","odota!","O-do-tah"],["do not go","älä mene","AH-lah MEH-neh"]],"ex":[["come here","tule tänne","TOO-leh TAHN-neh"],["do not come here","älä tule tänne","AH-lah TOO-leh TAHN-neh"],["sit down","istu alas","IS-too AH-lahs"],["do not sit down","älä istu","AH-lah IS-too"],["be quiet","ole hiljaa","O-leh HIL-yah"],["do not be late","älä myöhästy","AH-lah MEW-ur-hahs-tew"],["open the door","avaa ovi","AH-vah O-vi"],["close the window","sulje ikkuna","SOOL-yeh IK-koo-nah"],["listen to me","kuuntele minua","KOON-teh-leh MI-noo-ah"],["do not worry","älä huolehdi","AH-lah HWOH-leh-hdi"],["speak slowly","puhu hitaasti","POO-hoo HI-tahs-ti"],["wait a moment","odota hetki","O-do-tah HET-ki"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Osata / voida (can): osaan, voin + infinitive. Täytyy / pitää (must): minun täytyy mennä. Haluta (want): haluan mennä."],"rows":[["I can swim","osaan uida","O-sahn OO-ee-dah"],["I must go","minun täytyy mennä","MI-noon TAY-tew-ew MEN-nah"],["I want to go","haluan mennä","HAH-loo-ahn MEN-nah"],["may I?","saanko?","SAHN-ko"]],"ex":[["I can swim","osaan uida","O-sahn OO-ee-dah"],["I cannot swim","en osaa uida","en O-sah OO-ee-dah"],["can you help me?","voitko auttaa minua?","VOY-tko OW-tah-ah MI-noo-ah"],["we must go","meidän täytyy mennä","MAY-dan TAY-tew-ew MEN-nah"],["we must not go","meidän ei pidä mennä","MAY-dan ay PI-dah MEN-nah"],["I want to eat","haluan syödä","HAH-loo-ahn SEW-ur-dah"],["I do not want to eat","en halua syödä","en HAH-loo-ah SEW-ur-dah"],["you can come","voit tulla","VOY-t TOOL-lah"],["you cannot come","et voi tulla","et voy TOOL-lah"],["she wants to study","hän haluaa opiskella","hahn HAH-loo-ah OP-pis-kel-lah"],["I must work today","minun täytyy tehdä työtä tänään","MI-noon TAY-tew-ew TEH-hdah TEW-ur-tah TAH-nahn"],["you must not run","et saa juosta","et sah YWOS-tah"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Finnish uses endings, not words in front. Inside: -ssa / -ssä (in), -sta / -stä (out of), -han / -hin (into). Outside: -lla / -llä (on, at), -lta / -ltä (from), -lle (onto, to)."],"rows":[["in the house","talossa","TAH-los-sah"],["out of the house","talosta","TAH-los-tah"],["into the house","taloon","TAH-lon"],["at school","koulussa","KOW-loos-sah"],["on the table","pöydällä","PUR-ew-dahl-lah"],["to a friend","ystävälle","EWS-tah-vahl-leh"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","kirja on pöydällä","KIR-yah on PUR-ew-dahl-lah"],["the cat is under the table","kissa on pöydän alla","KIS-sah on PUR-ew-dahn AHL-lah"],["I am at school","olen koulussa","O-len KOW-loos-sah"],["I am at home","olen kotona","O-len KO-to-nah"],["the shop is next to the bank","kauppa on pankin vieressä","KOWP-pah on PAHN-kin VEE-eh-res-sah"],["the park is near the station","puisto on aseman lähellä","POO-ees-to on AH-seh-mahn LAH-hel-lah"],["we meet in the morning","tapaamme aamulla","TAH-pahm-meh AH-mool-lah"],["the lesson is at nine","tunti on yhdeksältä","TOON-ti on EWH-dek-sahl-tah"],["the key is in the bag","avain on laukussa","AH-vah-een on LOW-koos-sah"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -mpi for \"more\": iso, isompi. \"Than\" is \"kuin\". For \"the most\", add -in: isoin."],"rows":[["big, bigger","iso, isompi","I-so, I-som-pi"],["good, better","hyvä, parempi","HEW-vah, PAH-reh-mpi"],["small, smaller","pieni, pienempi","PEE-eh-ni, PEE-eh-nem-pi"],["the biggest","isoin","I-so-in"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","iso, isompi, isoin","I-so, I-som-pi, I-so-in"],["small, smaller, the smallest","pieni, pienempi, pienin","PEE-eh-ni, PEE-eh-nem-pi, PEE-eh-nin"],["this is better than that","tämä on parempi kuin tuo","TAH-mah on PAH-reh-mpi KOO-in TOO-oh"],["this is worse than that","tämä on huonompi kuin tuo","TAH-mah on HWOH-nom-pi KOO-in TOO-oh"],["she is taller than me","hän on pidempi kuin minä","hahn on PI-dem-pi KOO-in MI-nah"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Taškent on suurempi kuin Samarkand","TAHSH-kent on SOO-rem-pi KOO-in SAH-mar-kahnd"],["it is the cheapest","se on halvin","seh on HAHL-vin"],["the same as","sama kuin","SAH-mah KOO-in"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[["I am hungry","minulla on nälkä","MI-nool-lah on NAHL-kah"],["I am thirsty","minulla on jano","MI-nool-lah on YAH-no"],["I am cold","minulla on kylmä","MI-nool-lah on KEWL-mah"],["it is raining","sataa","SAH-tah"]],"ex":[["he is a teacher","hän on opettaja","hahn on OP-pet-tah-yah"],["you (plural) are students","te olette opiskelijoita","teh O-let-teh OP-pis-keh-li-yoy-tah"],["I am happy","olen onnellinen","O-len ON-nel-li-nen"],["she is at school","hän on koulussa","hahn on KOW-loos-sah"],["you are my friend","olet ystäväni","O-let EWS-tah-vah-ni"],["it is cold","on kylmä","on KEWL-mah"],["I study English","opiskelen englantia","OP-pis-keh-len EN-glahn-ti-ah"],["he teaches maths","hän opettaa matematiikkaa","hahn OP-pet-tah MAH-teh-mah-teek-kah"],["they work every day","he työskentelevät joka päivä","heh TEW-urs-ken-teh-leh-vaht YO-kah PAH-ee-vah"],["is this your book?","onko tämä sinun kirjasi?","ON-ko TAH-mah SI-noon KIR-yah-si"],["are they here?","ovatko he täällä?","O-vaht-ko heh TAH-ahl-lah"],["do you like tea?","pidätkö teestä?","PI-dat-ko TAYS-tah"],["what time is it?","paljonko kello on?","PAHL-yon-ko KEL-lo on"],["whose book is this?","kenen kirja tämä on?","KEH-nen KIR-yah TAH-mah on"],["how old are you?","kuinka vanha olet?","KOOEEN-kah VAHN-hah O-let"],["how do you say it?","miten se sanotaan?","MI-ten seh SAH-no-tahn"],["your book (formal)","teidän kirjanne","TAY-dahn KIR-yahn-neh"],["their house","heidän talonsa","HAY-dahn TAH-lon-sah"],["my phone","minun puhelimeni","MI-noon POO-heh-li-meh-ni"],["excuse me, sir","anteeksi, herra","AHN-tayk-si, HER-rah"],["please sit down (formal)","istukaa, olkaa hyvä","IS-too-kah, OL-kah HEW-vah"],["come here (informal)","tule tänne","TOO-leh TAHN-neh"],["yesterday I was tired","eilen olin väsynyt","AY-len O-lin VAH-sew-newt"],["I will study tomorrow","opiskelen huomenna","OP-pis-keh-len HWOH-men-nah"],["we went to the park","menimme puistoon","MEH-nim-meh POO-ees-ton"]]}],"name":"Finnish","id":"fi","flag":"fi","note":""}